{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,110p' frontier_605_verified.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Reproduction notes for the 605-action candidate\n\nAll observations below were reproduced through frames, advertised actions and\nclones. They do not establish that a 600-action solution is impossible.\n\n## Concrete result\n\n- `python verify_shorter_campaign.py` produced\n  `CAMPAIGN 9 moves 605 prefix 505 validated True`.\n- The candidate is `candidate_campaign_level9_605.json`; its prefix is\n  `candidate_prefix_level8_505.json`.\n- `GKM_FRESH_REPLAY=1 python gkm_try.py` still produced\n  `RESULT levels=8 moves=600 replay_ok=True err=RuntimeError: real-move/time cap`.\n- No writes to `checkpoint.json` were made.\n- `players.play_level_7` now composes existing legs for a clone-verified\n  132-action solution, replacing the previous 141-action solution.\n- `play_level_9` remains the existing 100-action composition. No new legs were\n  needed for the level 7 improvement.\n\n## Reproducing the new level 7 path\n\n1. `python verify_new_routes_clean.py 7 global` reproduces the current global\n   model candidate from a pristine level entry. Its final output was\n   `NEW_ROUTE_VERIFIED 7 7 132`.\n2. `candidate_level7_verified_132_clean.json` preserves the concrete screen\n   action path. `python integrate_screen_path.py 7\n   candidate_level7_verified_132_clean.json` independently checks the path and\n   the existing-leg composition before installing it.\n3. `python verify_shorter_campaign.py` replays the composed campaign on a clone\n   and calls the documented validator.\n\nThe saving comes from staging the second room's socket during the first room's\nferry trips while also planning the third room's mobile supports. An isolated\neight-move saving left the third room nine moves worse. The accepted route\nplans all three regions together.\n\n## Compact observations and bounded model searches\n\n- `observe9_clean.py LEVEL` replays the admitted 614-action predecessor on a\n  clone and collects symbolic objects and terrain. The files\n  `candidate_world{3,4,5,6,7,8,9}_reproduced.json` contain these observations.\n  It corrects camera translation using a unique blue helper on click actions;\n  blue helpers can themselves move with carriers on key actions.\n- The reproduced predecessor's boundaries were\n  `8,42,87,137,220,305,446,514,614`.\n- `search9_first_clean.py` found no route below 14 jumps to reduce the first\n  board and load its remaining yellow onto the socket.\n- `search9_top_clean.py` found a minimum of 28 jumps for the reproduced upper\n  board with two helpers, under the tested jump rules. This matches the player.\n- `optimize7_joint_clean.py` builds the 29,260 possible configurations of the\n  third room's four sockets (one empty, three carrying pink supports) and its\n  exact remaining cost table. Minimum tail cost in its phase model is 23.\n- `optimize7_global_clean.py` uses that table with the first and second room\n  carrier routes. `full` starts at the pristine entry; `full alternate` tries\n  delivering the helper first. Neither found a route below 132 within this\n  fixed sequence of boarding and unloading operations.\n- `candidate_level7_global_model_clean.json` is the accepted model route.\n  `candidate_level7_remaining_values_clean.pkl` caches the derived value table.\n- `fit7_initial_clean.py` filters possible hidden initial configurations\n  against reproduced observations. It currently retains 954 initial states,\n  but only four distinct images after the first seven keys. Accepted route\n  verification reached a single predicted tail configuration.\n- `identify_middle7_clean.py` reproduced that the second room socket initially\n  lies at either `(92,14)` or `(92,20)`; these candidates become equivalent\n  under the accepted initial route.\n\n## Falsified shortcuts and corrected interpretation\n\n- ACTION7 is **undo**, not reset. `probe_reset